Kinnan doubles every nonland mana source you tap. That is a ramp effect on paper and a combo engine in practice: Basalt Monolith taps for three, Kinnan makes it four, and untapping costs three. One mana profit per cycle, repeated as many times as you like. This is a Bracket 5 deck, so the counterspells are free, the mana is fast, and the game is expected to end on a single turn.

# The commander
Kinnan, Bonder Prodigy :: two mana. Every nonland permanent you tap for mana produces one extra of a type it made, and his {5}{G}{U} ability digs five deep and puts a non-Human creature straight onto the battlefield.
The activated ability is the payoff, not a mana sink. With unlimited mana you activate it over and over, assembling every relevant creature in the deck.
Delighted Halfling :: uncounterable mana for legendary spells, which is how Kinnan resolves through a table of blue decks.

# The infinite mana
Basalt Monolith :: taps for three, Kinnan makes it four, untaps for three. Net one per cycle, forever. Two cards, and the deck is built to find both.
Nyxbloom Ancient :: triples what any permanent produces. Basalt Monolith alone becomes nine mana against a three-mana untap — a second, independent infinite.
Grim Monolith :: mana-neutral with Kinnan rather than infinite, but it is still four mana off a two-drop and it fuels the turn you find the real piece.
Mana Vault :: three mana on turn one.
Dramatic Reversal :: untaps every nonland permanent. With Kinnan doubling a board of rocks and dorks it is an enormous one-shot ritual.
Seedborn Muse :: untaps everything on all three opponents' turns, which with Kinnan is three extra full mana pools per round.

# Turning mana into a win
Thrasios, Triton Hero :: {4} to scry and draw. With unlimited mana it draws your entire library, and it is a two-drop you can deploy on turn two.
Kinnan, Bonder Prodigy :: the {5}{G}{U} ability, activated repeatedly, puts every non-Human creature in the deck onto the battlefield.
Invasion of Ikoria :: fetches a non-Human creature from library OR graveyard onto the battlefield, and flips into Zilortha.
Zilortha, Apex of Ikoria :: every non-Human creature you control assigns combat damage as though unblocked. After a Kinnan dig chain, that is lethal to the table.
Hullbreaker Horror :: uncounterable, flash, and with unlimited spells it bounces every permanent your opponents control.
Finale of Devastation :: at X of ten or more, a tutor and a lethal team pump on one card.
Consecrated Sphinx :: two cards for every card any opponent draws — the fair game's engine.

# Finding the pieces
Green Sun's Zenith :: any green creature onto the battlefield, and X can be zero for Dryad Arbor-style plays or high for the payoff.
Chord of Calling :: instant speed, convoke, any creature.
Nature's Rhythm :: the same on a sorcery, with harmonize to buy it back.
Whir of Invention :: instant speed, improvise, any artifact — usually Basalt Monolith.
Transmute Artifact :: trades a rock for exactly the rock you need.
Trophy Mage :: fetches a three-mana artifact, which is Basalt Monolith.
Drift of Phantasms :: transmute for three, which is also Basalt Monolith — and it blocks fliers while you wait.
Formidable Speaker :: tutors a creature and untaps a permanent every turn.

# The copy package
Every one of these can become a second Basalt Monolith, a second Kinnan, or a copy of whatever an opponent just played.
Copy Artifact :: cheap, and it copies their Sol Ring as happily as your Monolith.
Mirrormade :: artifacts and enchantments.
Phyrexian Metamorph :: two life instead of blue mana, and it copies creatures too.
Clever Impersonator :: any nonland permanent.
Flesh Duplicate :: two mana for a copy of any creature.
Mockingbird :: scales, flies, and copies for exactly the mana you have.
Mirage Mirror :: becomes anything on the board for {2}, repeatedly, at instant speed.
Flash Photography :: a token copy of your own permanent at instant speed, twice with flashback.
Gilded Drake :: two mana to take their commander.

# Fast mana
Sol Ring :: turn one, every time.
Lotus Petal :: free, and Kinnan doubles it.
Mox Amber :: live the moment Kinnan or Thrasios resolves.
Mox Diamond :: a land for a Mox in a deck that does not need many lands.
Mox Opal :: metalcraft comes quickly here.
Chrome Mox :: fast, at the cost of a card.
Elvish Spirit Guide :: a free green from hand on turn one.
Birds of Paradise :: fixing that Kinnan doubles.
Llanowar Elves :: two green under Kinnan.
Elvish Mystic :: the second copy.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the third.
Springleaf Drum :: taps a summoning-sick dork for mana, doubled by Kinnan.
Gene Pollinator :: taps any permanent for mana, doubled.
Enduring Vitality :: every creature you control taps for any colour, and it comes back as an enchantment when it dies.
Badgermole Cub :: an extra green for every creature you tap for mana.
The Cabbage Merchant :: Food off their noncreature spells, and the Food taps for mana.

# Interaction
Force of Will :: the free counterspell that defines the format.
Force of Negation :: free on their turn against noncreature spells.
Pact of Negation :: free now; you win before the upkeep.
Fierce Guardianship :: free with your commander out.
Flusterstorm :: nearly unbeatable in a counter war.
Swan Song :: one mana for a wrath, a removal spell or an enchantment.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: the same for anything noncreature.
Mental Misstep :: two life for their turn-one accelerant.
Disrupting Shoal :: free, and it names their exact mana value.
Mindbreak Trap :: free against a storm turn, and it exiles.
Misdirection :: free, and it turns their removal or tutor into yours.
Commandeer :: free, and it steals their combo piece outright.
Veil of Summer :: one mana that beats blue and black interaction and draws.
Endurance :: free graveyard hate at instant speed, and a 3/4 reach blocker.
Chain of Vapor :: one mana to bounce anything, including your own permanent in response to removal.
Amphibian Downpour :: flash and storm — on a long turn it turns the table's commanders into 1/1 Frogs.

# Card flow
The One Ring :: a full turn of protection, then an escalating draw engine.
Rhystic Study :: their turns pay for yours.
Mystic Remora :: the strongest card in the deck on turns one through four.
Faerie Mastermind :: flash, flies, and draws off the table's extra draws.
Wan Shi Tong, Librarian :: scales, draws on entry, and punishes every tutor at the table.
Valley Floodcaller :: noncreature spells gain flash, and it untaps your creatures on each one.
High Fae Trickster :: everything gains flash, so the whole combo turn can happen on their end step.
Borne Upon a Wind :: the cheap version of the same effect, and it cantrips.
Agatha's Soul Cauldron :: exiles graveyards, hands out activated abilities, and lets you spend any colour on creature abilities.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep fast mana and interaction. A hand with Sol Ring or two Moxen plus a Force effect is a keep; a hand of value creatures is not. This deck expects to win around turn four and must survive somebody else trying to win on turn three.
Kinnan is the whole deck, so protect the cast. Delighted Halfling makes him uncounterable; otherwise hold a Force effect rather than jamming him into open blue mana.
Find Basalt Monolith, not a bigger creature. Trophy Mage, Drift of Phantasms, Whir of Invention and Transmute Artifact all point at the same three-mana rock, and it is the shortest path to unlimited mana.
Once mana is infinite, activate Kinnan before you cast anything from hand. The dig puts creatures straight onto the battlefield, which sidesteps every counterspell at the table.
